# The render goldens are byte-pinned render contracts: a windows checkout
# with core.autocrlf=true must never turn their LF bytes into CRLF, or the
# byte-compare in the golden tests fails with a phantom whole-file diff
# (run 43330792666). LF in the working tree on every platform.
**/testdata/*.txt text eol=lf
**/testdata/*.json text eol=lf

# The systemd templates are render sources pinned by regexp anchors
# (`(?m)^ExecStart=...$` in internal/cli): a windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true turns their LF bytes into CRLF and the `$` anchors
# never match (runs 43330792666 + 43339290411 — the testdata pin above
# missed the template dir). LF in the working tree on every platform.
systemd/*.service text eol=lf
systemd/README.md text eol=lf
